Attribution for extraction output
---------------------------------

CC BY 4.0 governs WTEM itself. It does not by itself reach the files WTEM
produces, so the following applies to them as an additional condition of use.

When you distribute the output of a WTEM run -- the language file, the
extraction report, or the generated companion data packs -- whether on its own
or inside a world you publish, state that those files were produced by WTEM and
give the attribution above (author, project URL, license). A line in the release
notes, the world's description, or a text file inside the save is enough.

This condition covers the generated files only. It makes no claim on the world
you extracted from, on your own translations of the extracted text, or on
anything else you distribute alongside them.
